WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Otome</i>:

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.840
A maiden, sweet-smelling as a flower,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.100
a single bud blooming in a tranquil
garden, pure and dignified.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.230
Too shy to even speak of love or romance,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.520
she dares not allow herself
to dream of a kiss.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.900
Even so, she blooms again today--

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.860
seeking, ever seeking
happiness beyond the stars.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.590
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.080
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.040
"Episode 2"
"Tamahiko Dies"

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:26.430
N-No! You mustn't!
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, don't look!

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.730
I... I'm not! I'm not looking!

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.570
"Taisho 11 (1922) - Early Spring"

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.650
I'm so sorry about earlier!

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.030
That was terribly disgraceful of me.

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:43.910
I-I didn't really see anything.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:48.460
The room was so steamy,
and I'm nearsighted...

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.960
It was all rather hazy.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.000
Well, thank goodness for that.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.050
Here: I've deboned your fish.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.970
Ah. Thank you.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.220
Isn't it delicious?

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.470
Too close!

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.360
You have rice on your face, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:20.240
Sure, she'll be my bride <i>someday</i>--

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.450
but to have such a young girl
looking after me like this...

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:30.500
That's right: I'm a pessimist who
hates all this world has to offer!

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.290
Good morning!

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.630
Special delivery for Mr. Tamahiko Shima.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.460
For me?

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.260
Who is it from?

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.880
"Tamayoshi Shima"

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.130
My father.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.850
"Tamaki and Tamayo have
received offers of marriage.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.060
But if the other families were to learn

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.650
of a younger brother

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:57.440
who lost use of his right hand,
quit school,

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:00.070
and is now holed up in the mountains,

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:04.820
it would bring shame on the
Shima family and ruin the matches.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:09.240
In order to better arrange these fine
marriages, I, as the Shima family head,

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.120
have decided that you will have
died in the accident instead.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.290
Consider it the sole act of familial duty
you are capable of carrying out."

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.220
Dinner is ready, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.730
I've made <i>hittsumi </i>dumpling soup.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:37.480
You like that, don't you, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:41.690
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>? Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.360
Please answer me!

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.240
I want to be left alone.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.490
But you didn't eat lunch...

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.370
<i>Please </i>just leave me alone!

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.880
No! That's Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>'s!

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.530
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.950
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.990
Pardon me.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:14.200
Your health will suffer if you
don't eat something already.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.410
I'll just leave it here.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.090
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.640
It's all right.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.310
You'll feel better soon.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:44.770
"Tamayoshi Shima"

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.320
Father! Father!

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.990
Don't touch me, dead man.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.950
The marriages will go forward,
thanks to you.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:01.830
The elder brother and sister bravely
enduring their brother's death...

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.170
It makes for <i>such </i>a beautiful story.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.550
Please--wait!

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:09.380
Father... my brother... my sister...

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.430
Tamao... Tamako!

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.510
I wish I were dead.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.440
I wish I were dead...

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.150
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?!

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:26.270
That's right...
I should just die for real.

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:30.990
It's all Father and my elder
siblings could ever want.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:33.280
Even <i>I </i>would be relieved.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.870
You should be lying down...

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.080
And you, Yuzu--
freed from your obligations.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:46.460
Just look at all the people who
stand to gain from me dying!

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:49.880
It's not like anyone cares about me...

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.480
Now, then... how to do the deed?

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:06.770
Hanging? Drowning? Poison?

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:09.940
A resentful death that
curses the whole world--

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:11.740
that'd be right up my alley.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.910
What's so funny?

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.490
I can't laugh at <i>any </i>of this!

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:26.670
I mean... I <i>have </i>to be laughing
to be able to say these things.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:31.550
For my own father to tell me
he's decided I'm dead...

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:33.880
"Tamayoshi Shima"

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:34.880
It's just...

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:37.430
It's just...

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:43.270
If the words are too painful
to say without wanting to cry,

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.100
you mustn't say them at all.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:49.820
If it hurt to be told
such terrible things,

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.440
whyever would you wound yourself further?

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.900
But...

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.700
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:04.330
Let it all out. You'll feel better.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:06.500
It's all right.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:14.220
There, there. I know it's hard.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.760
It's all right.

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:18.550
There, there.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.240
Yuzu...

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.160
Yuzu?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:58.010
♬ The bird doesn't fly,
but cries and cries ♬

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:03.850
♬ It's always crying, all alone ♬

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.310
♬ In the shadow-- ♬

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.940
Ta-Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?!

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.230
You really should rest a little more...

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.860
Sleeping in there all alone got... boring.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.120
Did you get <i>lonely</i>?

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:22.490
"Urk"

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:26.580
What?! Why would I? That's just...

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.540
Here, give me your forehead.

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:39.680
Uh-huh! Your fever seems
to have gone down.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:42.050
You'll get cold in the kitchen.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:45.390
Put this on and sit by the fire.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.850
The rice porridge will be ready soon.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.690
Don't overdo it, now.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:59.950
I ruined her best outfit,
and not a single word of complaint.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.160
"sting sting"

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.160
You're not cold?

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:07.910
Tokyo...

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:11.750
Let's... let's go to Tokyo--together!

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.470
What a stylish building!

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:28.520
So this is Tokyo Station--

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.140
gateway to the Imperial Palace!

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.730
Everyone's just so chic!

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.570
All these men and women,
dressed à la mode!

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:44.160
--So many people looking so cute...
--Why did I come here, exactly?

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:48.160
--Everywhere I look!
--I thought I'd never leave the house again.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.210
It's nice to spread your
wings once in a while.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:54.000
That brings back bad memories...

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.000
It's all so bright,
it makes your head spin!

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.010
Right, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:04.300
But I have to make amends.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.850
Okay--let's go.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:13.770
Oh, wow. Oh, wow! Oh, <i>wow</i>!

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:39.170
It's like a dream come true!

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:44.380
So many--and these are just
the fancy collars!

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:49.010
And all this cloth, too!

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.970
--They're all glorious!
--She's like a little kid.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.730
Please let me know if there's
something you're looking for.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:01.400
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>? Um...

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.990
Are you sure about this?

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:09.080
It's my fault your kimono was ruined.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.160
Thank you so much!

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:14.620
Then if you insist...
I don't mind if I do!

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.830
--Is there something you could recommend?
--It's just too pitiful to have only
the clothes on your back.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:20.000
--Let's see... This one is very popular.
--It's just too pitiful to have only
the clothes on your back.

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:31.720
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.310
Which do you prefer?

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:41.610
I like the light pink of this one.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:44.650
But the lavender one is nice, too.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:47.860
Aren't they both wonderful?

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:51.490
Oh, what to do...

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:52.950
Shall we buy both?

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.580
What?!

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:59.130
We can't! I already feel bad
that you're buying me <i>anything</i>!

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:03.050
This one's 12 yen, that one's 10...

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:08.640
And they're eye-poppingly expensive, too!

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.470
It's all right. Money I have.

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:13.520
All right--we'll take both.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:15.390
Thank you very much!

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:22.360
I'm so grateful, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:27.740
I've never owned such fine fabric.
I'm in seventh heaven!

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:30.820
For her to be this happy....

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.080
Um...

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.120
I'm sorry.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:42.630
I did something to your kimono
that couldn't be undone.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:47.380
Did it have any sentimental
meaning for you?

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.090
Meaning...?

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:53.600
Now that you mention it, it was
the first one I'd ever sewn.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:59.600
I knew it! What I did really
<i>can't </i>be undone!

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:02.190
No new kimono can ever replace <i>that</i>!

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:05.650
But it's all right.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:12.120
The fabric you bought for me
is all I can think about now.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:18.910
One day this will be the first
kimono my lover ever bought me,

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:22.960
then the first my husband
ever bought me...

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:27.090
It'll be precious to me
all throughout my life.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.590
Maybe I'll be giving it to a daughter
or granddaughter one day.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:38.980
How can she say something so
embarrassing without blushing?

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:44.520
What gives? I apologized
to her and everything.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:45.900
Ugh!

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.190
Who cares?

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:52.740
I'm going to make one
outstanding kimono with this!

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.240
It's just so adorable...

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:58.660
Like something Kotori Shiratori
would wear.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:15:59.750
Shiratori?

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:05.710
You haven't heard of her?
She's a singer: Kotori Shiratori.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:08.670
She's cute, plays all sorts
of instruments--

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.840
and her voice is just beautiful.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.390
She was terribly popular
at the girls' school.

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:28.020
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>! An escalator!
We have to ride it!

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.700
"Perfume"
"Please Try"

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:49.130
Oh! That building--Ryounkaku!

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:05.480
Yuzu?

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:08.820
"I want" "ice cream"

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:14.530
Here you are.

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:15.910
Take your time and enjoy!

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:23.000
Ice cream in a department-store
food hall... so fancy!

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.000
Delectable!

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:38.430
I'm surprised you can eat such cold
stuff when it's still chilly outside.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:41.220
It's delicious. Try some!

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.220
Say "ah"!

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.100
My, how positively vulgar!

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:49.110
Young people these days...

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:53.570
--Why, back in our day,
we had manners and class!
--Stop that! People are looking at us!

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:55.110
--Why, back in our day,
we had manners and class!
--I-I'm sorry...

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:58.740
--We did indeed!
--I-I felt like I was back at school...

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:01.490
Don't treat me like one
of your girlfriends!

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:07.460
Honestly... and all because
we came to Tokyo.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:13.050
But at least Yuzu seems
to be enjoying herself.

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:14.710
That's good enough.

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:16.550
Here goes!

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.590
How is it? Good?

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:20.140
Yeah--<i>real </i>good!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.390
That's great!

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.060
Eat plenty, now.

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:35.400
I have decided that you will have died.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:42.200
Thanks for the ice cream.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:45.290
It was so incredibly delicious.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:51.580
Now, then--shall we? We don't want
to be late for our train home.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:52.920
Oh... right.

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:02.640
When I left my parents...

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:08.180
I told them to think of me as being dead.

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:14.190
But I wouldn't <i>actually </i>die, of course.

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:18.450
We would never meet again,
as if death had parted us,

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:22.120
but I would be out there living
in happiness somewhere.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.660
So went my thinking.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.660
Impressive thought process.

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:34.710
It's easier on you mentally
when you think positive!

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:40.930
Sometimes the things
Yuzu says point to the truth.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.600
T-Too close!

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:02.950
It's all right. I'll always be
right here beside you...

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:04.320
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:22.090
After that, Yuzu worked on her
kimono in every spare moment.

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:29.810
"One Month Later"

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:31.140
It's finished!

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:34.020
What do you think?

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:41.650
Well? Isn't it terribly grown-up?

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:42.650
Eh?

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:45.320
Grown... <i>up</i>?

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.700
You can let it out at the
shoulders, like a child's!

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:52.410
Well? Well? Don't I look like Kotori?

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:58.380
Why, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, you're <i>captivated</i>!

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:01.090
I--I most certainly am not!

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.300
It's perfectly fine. Don't be embarrassed.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:04.340
I'm <i>not</i>!

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:13.440
Greetings and salutations,

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.480
big brother Tamahiko.

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:22.070
You're not like you were back home.

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:24.360
You certainly seem
to be enjoying yourself.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:29.200
So you can talk to girls now, I see.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:32.500
What... what are you doing here?

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:34.290
Who might that be?

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:36.040
My little sister Tamako.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.540
What?!

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:40.550
Bring my things inside.

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:42.380
Yes'm!

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:46.590
Hey, what's with all the baggage?
Why'd you come here, anyway?

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:49.680
I came to enjoy the family villa.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:53.600
This is my <i>home </i>now!
You can't just drop by!

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.850
What do <i>you </i>know? <i>You're </i>dead.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:01.980
Perhaps I'll move here myself...

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:43.380
Tamako-<i>san </i>is so beautiful and demure!

00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:48.970
But... I don't think she likes me
or Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>very much.
